```java
public class BankAccount {
    private static int counter;            // shared
    private static final String BANK = "GlobalBank"; // static constant
    private final String accountNumber;

    static { counter = 1000; }             // runs once at class load

    public BankAccount() {
        this.accountNumber = BANK + "-" + (counter++);
    }
    public static int created() { return counter - 1000; } // static method
}
```

```java
class Dog extends Animal {
    Dog(String name) {
        System.out.println("creating"); // COMPILE ERROR: must come after super()
        super(name);                    // super() must be the FIRST statement
    }
}
```

```java
class Dog extends Animal {
    private String breed;
    Dog(String name, String breed) {
        super(name);        // FIRST statement — initializes the parent
        this.breed = breed; // 'this' disambiguates field from parameter
    }
}
```
`this()` and `super()` are mutually exclusive — only one can be the first statement of a constructor.

```java
abstract class Animal {
    abstract String sound(); // no body — subclasses must implement
}
Animal a = new Animal(); // COMPILE ERROR: can't instantiate an abstract class
```

```java
abstract class Animal {
    abstract String sound();
    String describe() { return "makes " + sound(); } // concrete + abstract mix
}
class Dog extends Animal {
    @Override String sound() { return "woof"; }
}
Animal a = new Dog();             // OK — instantiate a concrete subclass
System.out.println(a.describe()); // makes woof
```

```java
